course: dictionary
lesson: 9069
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by looking at the words around it, which is the context. Slipper is a good example.
explain: «Ollie in Bristol put a rubber spider in his dad's slipper.» Here a slipper is a soft shoe you wear indoors, because you put your foot inside it at home.
explain: In stories, a slipper can be something special. Cinderella's glass slipper fits only her, so the story is about a magic shoe, not one you wear around the house.
explain: Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If the glass slipper were a shoe for the house, the story would not work.
fact: A slipper is a soft, comfortable shoe you wear indoors.
fact: Cinderella's glass slipper is a famous slipper from a fairy tale.
fact: Slippers come in pairs: a pair of slippers means two slippers.
fact: So 5 pairs of slippers means 10 slippers.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one.
exercise: «Put on your slippers before you sit down.» What is a slipper here? | * A soft shoe you wear indoors | A type of sock for football | A glass shoe from a fairy tale | A kind of bed
exercise: Maths: 5 pairs of slippers. How many slippers is that? | * 10 | 5 | 15 | 2
exercise: «Cinderella's glass slipper fits only her.» Which slipper is this? | A slipper for the rain | A slipper for wearing at home | A slipper for the gym | * A glass slipper from a fairy tale
test: «Then "qǐng jìn" (come in, please), and your eyes go to the row of slippers by the door: huàn tuōxié, change into slippers.» What does the sentence tell you to do? | * Change your shoes for slippers | Go out into the rain | Put a glass slipper on a shelf | Buy a new pair of trainers
test: «Working from home means doing a job at home with a computer; the parent is still at work and needs quiet, even in slippers.» In this sentence, what are slippers? | Glass shoes from a story | A type of work | A kind of computer | * Soft shoes worn at home
exam: In «a pair of slippers», how many slippers are there? | One | Four | Ten | * Two
